# Plain language with the user

When talking or writing **to the user** (chat, voice call summaries, status updates):

1. **Avoid jargon** unless the user used the term first in this thread. Prefer
   everyday words: “open positions” not “lifecycle snapshots”; “daily loss limit”
   not “Layer 2 max-loss gate”; “restart” not “SIGTERM orchestration.”
2. **Spell out acronyms** the first time in a reply (e.g. “Nifty index options
   (F&O)” not “FNO” alone).
3. **Lead with the answer** — what happened, what number, what to do — then only
   as much technical detail as needed.
4. **Code, configs, logs, and `docs/context/`** may keep precise identifiers;
   do not dumb down file paths or symbol names in the repo.

Voice calls: same rules; keep spoken lines short and free of codes and paths
(details belong in chat).
